--TEST--
`Core\Router::match` answers the compiled table for a verb and a path the program picked, and `null` where no route claims that pair — `rule:routing/matched-once-before-the-handler`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: Core\Http\Method
// § 1 puts the *request's* match on the request: the door takes it once, before
// any of this program ran, and `Core\Request::route()` hands that one back.
// This member is the other question entirely -- asked of the table, about a
// verb and a path the caller chose -- which is why a CLI program can ask it at
// all. Matching still dispatches nothing: neither method below is called.
class Pages
{
    #[Core\Route(path:"/pages/{slug}", method: Core\Http\Method::Get, name: "Pages::show")]
    #[Core\Access(allow: Core\Audience::Public)]
    public function show(string $slug): string
    {
        return $slug;
    }

    #[Core\Route(path:"/pages", method: Core\Http\Method::Post, name: "Pages::create")]
    #[Core\Access(allow: Core\Audience::Public)]
    public function create(): string
    {
        return "made";
    }
}

// A hit answers the name the `#[Route]` declared, which is the unit's own text
// and never anything the caller supplied.
?Core\Router\Match $shown = Core\Router::match(Core\Http\Method::Get, "/pages/intro");
if ($shown != null) {
    echo "name: ", $shown->name() ?? "unnamed", "\n";
}

// The same path under another verb is a different route, not the same one
// asked differently -- so a `Post` at a `Get`-only path claims nothing.
?Core\Router\Match $posted = Core\Router::match(Core\Http\Method::Post, "/pages/intro");
if ($posted == null) {
    echo "post at a get-only path: null", "\n";
}

// And the verb that does claim its own path answers a route with no captures.
?Core\Router\Match $created = Core\Router::match(Core\Http\Method::Post, "/pages");
if ($created != null) {
    echo "name: ", $created->name() ?? "unnamed", "\n";
    echo "captures: ", Core\Arr::count($created->params()) as string, "\n";
}

// A path no row claims at all is `null`, which is the answer a `404` is decided
// from -- `Core\Router::methodsFor` is the member that tells it from a `405`.
?Core\Router\Match $missing = Core\Router::match(Core\Http\Method::Get, "/nowhere");
if ($missing == null) {
    echo "unclaimed path: null", "\n";
}
--EXPECT--
name: Pages::show
post at a get-only path: null
name: Pages::create
captures: 0
unclaimed path: null
